{
    "test_name": "MOB.547_AssetVerify_Photo_Tag_Search",
    "details": {
        "name": "MOB.547_AssetVerify_Photo_Tag_Search",
        "type": "browser",
        "status": "paused",
        "message": "`MOB.547` **The tag search's create button is an exclusive-or with an exact match** \u2014\nchecklist \ud83d\udfe2 #18, covering `db95798d54` (2026-09-10).\n- READ-ONLY. It sets the search input's value and reads the dropdown. Selecting an option\n  assigns a tag and the create option posts a new one, so neither is ever clicked; it\n  leaves through `Done`.\n- \u2b50 **The rule changed from *no results* to *no EXACT match*.** A partial term now shows\n  results **and** the create button \u2014 impossible before. Three probes close it:\n  `Batter` \u2192 `Battery Pack` listed **and** create offered \u00b7 `  cUSTOM  ` \u2192\n  `Custom` matched, two options listed, create **gone** \u00b7 `ZZZZ-NO-SUCH-TAG` \u2192 no options,\n  create offered.\n- The padded, mis-cased `  cUSTOM  ` also proves the `trim().toLocaleLowerCase()`\n  normalisation, on a search that still returns results \u2014 so *results exist* and *create\n  hidden* are shown to be independent.\n- \ud83d\uded1 The tag badge is a NAME badge when the photo has 1\u20133 tags and only reads\n  `Edit Tags (n)` otherwise (`PhotoMenu.tsx:154-181`), so it is targeted by the green\n  outline the component itself sets, not by that text.\n- Runs on `MOB.546`'s route (AV asset detail \u2192 Attachments \u2192 Photos).",
        "tags": [
            "Mobile",
            "env:dev",
            "Asset Verification",
            "Photos",
            "read-only"
        ],
        "locations": [
            "gcp:us-west2"
        ],
